    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488">

                <pb facs="0597" n="587" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg587"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/6–2948: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-06-29T10:00:00+09:00">June 29, 1948—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 29—2:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1174. Foreign Office has informed Embassy it will require 48 hours after complete
                    agreement of English text to prepare Chinese document for simultaneous
                    signature. (RefEmbtel 1171 June 28 and Embtel 1154 June 25).<anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d488-f1"/> Embassy check Chinese text must follow which places
                    effective deadline as late June 30 or early July 1.</p>
                <p>In event impasse which now looms reference articles III and IV, how seriously
                    would Department assess repercussions and consequences of failure reach and sign
                    agreement by statutory date July 3?</p>
                <p>Sent Department 1174, repeated Shanghai 543.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
